# Helios, a trustee's decryption proof: the same secret key opens the
# published key and produces the decryption factor.  Proving both with
# one x is what stops a trustee decrypting with a key other than the
# one it published, and the compiler merging the conjunction into a
# single leaf is what ties them together -- two equations reading the
# same column.  Examples/Helios.v, decrypt_stmt.
secrets x
claims  x
eq  pk   g
eq  M    AA

# An instance: one distinct generator per base name, so the
# environment is faithful and the verdict above transfers to it.
# The exponents are ours and carry no meaning; every element of a
# prime-order group is a generator power, so this is simply a way
# to write distinct elements down.
point g   2
point AA  3
